  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Philippines Typhoon Goni</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On Sunday 1st Nov, Typhoon Goni - categorised as the world&#x2019;s strongest tropical cyclone in 2020 so far &#x2013; made landfall in the Philippines. First hitting in Bato, Catanduanes, and then again in Tiwi, Albay, the typhoon brought with it catastrophic violent winds and torrential rainfall. With maximum sustained winds of more than 251 kilometers per hour, the equivalent of a Category 5 Hurricane, its effects have been devastating. Over 402,000 families have been affected and, so far, 17 deaths have been confirmed. Power and communications remain out in many areas, but while the full extent of the damage is yet to be seen, initial reports indicate that many houses were severely damaged or destroyed, with some houses being totally washed out along the coastline.
&#xA0;
The Philippine Red Cross (PRC) has already launched their emergency response, deploying teams to support the search and rescue efforts and assist survivors</narrative>
  </description>
